# PR Suggestion Triage and Reply Workflow

For PR ${1:PR_URL_OR_NUMBER}, review every suggestion thread and choose one outcome before changing code.

## 1. Classify each suggestion

| Thread | Suggestion | Actually issue? | Introduced here? | Fix now? | Not applicable? | Follow-up? | Reason |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| ${2:thread/link} | ${3:summary} | ${4:yes/no} | ${5:yes/no} | ${6:yes/no} | ${7:yes/no} | ${8:yes/no} | ${9:reason} |

## 2. Pick the action

### A. Fix in this PR
Use when the issue was introduced here, is blocking, is small/low-risk, or affects packaging, CI, tests, dependencies, typing consistency, or obvious correctness.

Before replying: implement, test, push if linking GitHub code, and confirm CI where relevant.

Reply format for code changes:
Updated ${10:short description of change} here:

${11:path/to/file}

Lines ${12:start} to ${13:end} in ${14:commit}

```python
${15:relevant code snippet}
```

Resolve only after the reply is posted and the fix is verified.

### B. Not applicable
Use when the suggestion does not apply, the code is stale, the path is already handled, the condition cannot occur, or the change would be incorrect.

Reply: This does not apply here because ${16:short reason}, as shown by ${17:CODE_LINK_WITH_LINE}.
Alternative: I checked this path and it is already handled here: ${18:CODE_LINK_WITH_LINE}.
Resolve only after the reply is posted and the evidence is clear.

### C. Create follow-up issue
Use when the suggestion is valid but broader than this PR, changes behaviour/architecture, is tech debt/uplift, was pre-existing, or would expand scope too much.

Issue body:
Follow-up from PR ${19:PR_NUMBER} review.

Context: ${20:short context}
Relevant code: ${21:CODE_OR_SOURCE_LINK_WITH_LINE}
Original PR review comment:
> ${22:PASTE_REVIEW_COMMENT_VERBATIM}

Reply: Created ${23:ISSUE_LINK} to track this as a follow-up since ${24:short reason}.
If carried over: Created ${25:ISSUE_LINK} to track this follow-up since the ${26:behaviour/pattern} was directly carried over from ${27:SOURCE_LINK_WITH_LINE}.
Resolve only after the issue exists, is labelled, and is linked in the thread.

## 3. Reply and resolve rules
Replies must be one sentence, generic, professional, non-defensive, posted in the original thread, and linked to code, issue, or evidence.
Resolve only when fixed and verified, confirmed not applicable with evidence, or tracked in a labelled follow-up issue.

$0
